<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<h3>Which chemistry should I start with?</h3>
<p>Start with the duty cycle and the temperature window. LFP is the default for stationary and cost-sensitive cycling; NMC is chosen when energy density or cold performance matters more than cycle life; LTO is a niche for high power and very low temperature.</p>
<h3>Do I need a BMS for a small pack?</h3>
<p>Yes. Every lithium pack needs cell-level protection against overcharge, over-discharge and over-temperature. A small pack can use a simpler BMS, but it cannot safely omit one.</p>
